/// \class RunOffMapBehavior
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_b
/// \brief Behavior module registered as "RunOffMapBehavior": when
///        triggered, orders its object to move to a named waypoint, or to a
///        point straight ahead, and then to die or be removed.
///
/// RunOffMapBehavior::triggerFlee starts the flight. It does nothing when
/// the object has no AI. The destination is the waypoint named by
/// \c RunOffMapWaypointName when the terrain logic finds a waypoint of that
/// name; otherwise it is a point a fixed distance ahead of the object along
/// its facing (500 world units in the BFME 2 body), at ground height. When
/// the pathfinder finds no path to the destination, the object is killed
/// on the spot. Otherwise the object's AI is given a move-and-die order
/// when \c DieOnMap is set and a move-and-delete order when it is not, and
/// the function also sets a status and a model condition on the object
/// that are not described here. RunOffMapBehavior::triggerFlee does not
/// read \c RunToLocation.
///
/// Another virtual function of the module, whose role is not described
/// here, calls RunOffMapBehavior::triggerFlee only when
/// \c RequiresSpecificTrigger is not set; what else calls it is not
/// described here either. The module registers an empty interface mask.
/// BFME 1 already has the class; Zero Hour does not.
///
/// \par Modding
/// - Own fields: \c RunToLocation (a 2D coordinate),
///   \c RequiresSpecificTrigger and \c DieOnMap (booleans) and
///   \c RunOffMapWaypointName (a waypoint name stored as text).
/// - A map that lacks the waypoint is not detected while the INI loads,
///   and it is not an error when the flight starts either: the object
///   heads for the point straight ahead instead, and is killed if no path
///   leads there. That fallback distance is hard-coded.
///
/// \see RunOffMapBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      RunOffMapBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class RunOffMapBehaviorModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_b
/// \brief Module data for RunOffMapBehavior: destination and trigger
///        settings.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// RunOffMapBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData and shared by every
/// object of the template.

/// \fn Module *RunOffMapBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "RunOffMapBehavior": creates the
