/// \class ShareExperienceBehavior
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_b
/// \brief Behavior module registered as "ShareExperienceBehavior": passes
///        an amount of experience on to nearby objects that pass an object
///        filter, multiplied by \c Percentage and, optionally, by a
///        distance falloff.
///
/// The sharing is done by another virtual function of the module, which
/// receives the amount to share. What calls it, and so which experience
/// gains are shared, is not described here; the class name suggests the
/// gains of the module's own object. ShareExperienceBehavior::update does
/// none of this work: it returns the sleep-forever value, so it does not
/// run again unless something wakes the module. When the sharing function
/// runs:
/// - Nothing is shared when \c Percentage is zero or less, or while the
///   object has a certain status.
/// - The recipients come from a range search of radius \c Radius around
///   the object: objects other than this one that pass \c ObjectFilter and
///   fixed checks not described here, and that have an experience tracker
///   which accepts experience. Further checks, one of them on a template
///   flag, can skip a recipient; they are not described here.
/// - Each recipient gets the amount multiplied by \c Percentage and by a
///   distance factor, when the result is above zero. \c DropOff is a
///   switch, not an amount: when it equals 1, the factor is 1 minus the
///   distance between the two objects' positions divided by \c Radius, so
///   it falls linearly to zero at \c Radius and never goes below zero; for
///   any other value the factor is 1 and there is no falloff.
/// - The multiplied amount is carried from one recipient to the next
///   instead of starting again from the original amount, so when there is
///   more than one recipient the factors compound, in the order the range
///   search returns the recipients.
///
/// BFME 1 already has the class; Zero Hour does not.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Own fields: \c Radius, \c DropOff and \c Percentage (reals) and
/// \c ObjectFilter (an object filter). \c Percentage is read as a plain
/// real and used directly as a multiplier: 1, the constructor default,
/// passes the full amount. \c DropOff turns the falloff on only when it is
/// exactly 1; its constructor default of 0, like any value other than 1,
/// means no falloff. Because the amount compounds from one recipient to the
/// next, a \c Percentage or falloff below 1 gives later recipients less
/// than earlier ones.
///
/// \see ShareExperienceBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      ShareExperienceBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class ShareExperienceBehaviorModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_b
/// \brief Module data for ShareExperienceBehavior: radius, drop-off,
///        percentage and filter.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// ShareExperienceBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData and shared by
/// every object of the template.

/// \fn Module *ShareExperienceBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "ShareExperienceBehavior":
///        creates the module for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration. The group
/// page describes the shared frame.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's ShareExperienceBehaviorModuleData.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see ShareExperienceBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *ShareExperienceBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "ShareExperienceBehavior": creates
///        the module data and parses the module's INI block into it.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration
/// for each module line naming the module. The group page describes the
/// shared frame; the class's \c buildFieldParse adds one table.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see ShareExperienceBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance


