/// \class SiegeDockingBehavior
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_b
/// \brief Behavior module registered as "SiegeDockingBehavior"; by its
///        name, it handles siege units docking at its object (not confirmed
///        here).
///
/// Its members include SiegeDockingBehavior::stopDocking,
/// SiegeDockingBehavior::xfer and SiegeDockingBehavior::loadPostProcess.
/// This page does not describe what the module does with its object or
/// with other units. BFME 1 already has the class; Zero Hour does not.
///
/// \par Modding
/// The data class's one field is \c DUMMY, read as an integer; nothing is
/// configured through it as far as this page establishes.
///
/// \par Saves
/// The module saves its own state (SiegeDockingBehavior::xfer) and runs its
/// own post-load step (SiegeDockingBehavior::loadPostProcess) before the
/// base class's; what that step restores is not described here.
///
/// \see SiegeDockingBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      SiegeDockingBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class SiegeDockingBehaviorModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_behavior_module_factories_b
/// \brief Module data for SiegeDockingBehavior: one integer field named
///        \c DUMMY.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// SiegeDockingBehaviorModuleData::friend_newModuleData and shared by
/// every object of the template.

/// \fn Module *SiegeDockingBehavior::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "SiegeDockingBehavior": creates
///        the module for one object.
///
